{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792332655,"nonce":"3ZK9UwW5Mi301ueObHapLlIyewg=","message":"Items 3 and 4 are done in 2b07f451 (local): FillRule in blinc_core, DrawContext::set_clip_fill_rule taken by the next push_clip, the rule in clip_radius.x of a polygon clip, and all twelve calculate_polygon_clip_alpha copies honouring it. Checked by pixels on a pentagram (the middle is filled nonzero, a hole even-odd). Items 1 and 2 are not done: ClipPath::Polygon and ::Path carry no rule, and the CSS parser takes no evenodd keyword. Adding the field to those variants breaks blinc_abi, which matches them without a rest pattern and carries even-odd separately (set_clip_even_odd), so it wants a change on both sides. Seen while testing: a self-intersecting polygon clip shows faint seams along the inner edges under nonzero, because the clip's edge anti-aliasing uses the distance to the nearest edge whether or not it bounds the inside. Also: GpuRenderer::render_msaa never uploaded the aux buffer (45f456df), so polygon clips did not draw through it.","files":null}]}